WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.083
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online B one, Book two.

2
00:00:05.383 --> 00:00:09.037
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.337 --> 00:00:15.031
Unit thirteen: Travel Basics. Today you will make predictions about trips with will.

4
00:00:15.331 --> 00:00:18.018
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:18.967 --> 00:00:22.455
Part one: words. You will learn twelve new words.

6
00:00:23.317 --> 00:00:24.585
Itinerary.

7
00:00:25.583 --> 00:00:28.953
Itinerary means a plan of a journey with places and times.

8
00:00:29.550 --> 00:00:31.805
Our itinerary has five cities.

9
00:00:32.417 --> 00:00:34.848
Your turn. Say: Itinerary.

10
00:00:37.700 --> 00:00:38.806
Itinerary.

11
00:00:39.550 --> 00:00:40.760
Passport.

12
00:00:41.750 --> 00:00:45.282
Passport means an official document for travel to other countries.

13
00:00:45.883 --> 00:00:47.523
Don't forget your passport!

14
00:00:48.117 --> 00:00:51.106
Your turn. Say: Passport.

15
00:00:53.967 --> 00:00:54.863
Passport.

16
00:00:55.617 --> 00:00:56.351
Visa.

17
00:00:57.350 --> 00:00:59.756
Visa means permission to enter a country.

18
00:01:00.350 --> 00:01:02.024
Do we need a visa for Thailand?

19
00:01:02.617 --> 00:01:05.687
Your turn. Say: Visa.

20
00:01:08.533 --> 00:01:09.511
Visa.

21
00:01:10.250 --> 00:01:11.437
Accommodation.

22
00:01:12.450 --> 00:01:15.506
Accommodation means a place to stay, like a hotel.

23
00:01:16.117 --> 00:01:17.803
We booked cheap accommodation.

24
00:01:18.417 --> 00:01:21.197
Your turn. Say: Accommodation.

25
00:01:24.033 --> 00:01:25.348
Accommodation.

26
00:01:26.083 --> 00:01:27.119
Departure.

27
00:01:28.117 --> 00:01:30.209
Departure means the time when you leave.

28
00:01:30.817 --> 00:01:32.712
Our departure is at 7 a.m.

29
00:01:33.317 --> 00:01:35.981
Your turn. Say: Departure.

30
00:01:38.833 --> 00:01:39.985
Departure.

31
00:01:40.750 --> 00:01:41.716
Layover.

32
00:01:42.717 --> 00:01:45.691
Layover means a short stop between two flights.

33
00:01:46.283 --> 00:01:48.678
We had a two-hour layover in Bangkok.

34
00:01:49.283 --> 00:01:52.040
Your turn. Say: Layover.

35
00:01:54.900 --> 00:01:55.878
Layover.

36
00:01:56.617 --> 00:01:57.722
Destination.

37
00:01:58.717 --> 00:02:01.471
Destination means the place you are travelling to.

38
00:02:02.083 --> 00:02:04.060
Our destination is Singapore.

39
00:02:04.650 --> 00:02:07.000
Your turn. Say: Destination.

40
00:02:09.867 --> 00:02:10.949
Destination.

41
00:02:11.683 --> 00:02:12.812
Souvenir.

42
00:02:13.817 --> 00:02:16.942
Souvenir means something you buy to remember a place.

43
00:02:17.550 --> 00:02:19.677
I bought a souvenir for my sister.

44
00:02:20.283 --> 00:02:23.307
Your turn. Say: Souvenir.

45
00:02:26.167 --> 00:02:27.179
Souvenir.

46
00:02:27.917 --> 00:02:28.813
Backpack.

47
00:02:29.817 --> 00:02:32.443
Backpack means a bag you carry on your back.

48
00:02:33.050 --> 00:02:35.575
Pack light. Just one backpack.

49
00:02:36.183 --> 00:02:38.662
Your turn. Say: Backpack.

50
00:02:41.500 --> 00:02:42.501
Backpack.

51
00:02:43.250 --> 00:02:44.843
Currency exchange.

52
00:02:45.850 --> 00:02:49.893
Currency exchange means changing money from one country's money to another.

53
00:02:50.483 --> 00:02:53.354
Find a currency exchange at the airport.

54
00:02:53.950 --> 00:02:57.543
Your turn. Say: Currency exchange.

55
00:03:00.400 --> 00:03:01.633
Currency exchange.

56
00:03:02.383 --> 00:03:03.419
Sightseeing.

57
00:03:04.417 --> 00:03:07.763
Sightseeing means visiting famous places as a tourist.

58
00:03:08.350 --> 00:03:10.419
We went sightseeing in the old town.

59
00:03:11.017 --> 00:03:13.379
Your turn. Say: Sightseeing.

60
00:03:16.233 --> 00:03:17.246
Sightseeing.

61
00:03:17.983 --> 00:03:18.926
Adventure.

62
00:03:19.917 --> 00:03:23.298
Adventure means an exciting, unusual experience.

63
00:03:23.883 --> 00:03:25.894
The jungle trek was an adventure.

64
00:03:26.483 --> 00:03:28.845
Your turn. Say: Adventure.

65
00:03:31.700 --> 00:03:32.771
Adventure.

66
00:03:33.567 --> 00:03:37.206
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

67
00:03:38.050 --> 00:03:39.991
Visal, where would you love to travel?

68
00:03:41.083 --> 00:03:44.130
Japan! I think it will be an amazing adventure.

69
00:03:45.217 --> 00:03:46.357
What will you need?

70
00:03:47.450 --> 00:03:52.157
I'll need a passport and a visa. I'll check them early.

71
00:03:53.250 --> 00:03:54.402
What will you do there?

72
00:03:55.517 --> 00:04:00.221
I'll go sightseeing in Kyoto, and I'm sure the food will be delicious!

73
00:04:01.367 --> 00:04:02.983
Part three: grammar.

74
00:04:03.817 --> 00:04:07.395
Grammar focus: Future with will for predictions.

75
00:04:07.695 --> 00:04:08.952
Look at the pattern.

76
00:04:09.650 --> 00:04:11.464
We will visit many places.

77
00:04:12.350 --> 00:04:14.036
The trip will be an adventure.

78
00:04:14.950 --> 00:04:16.741
I think it will rain in Tokyo.

79
00:04:17.700 --> 00:04:22.175
Use 'will' for predictions and quick decisions. Short form: I'll, it'll, we'll.

80
00:04:22.917 --> 00:04:26.393
Be careful! Don't say: The trip will is an adventure.

81
00:04:28.333 --> 00:04:30.704
Say: The trip will be an adventure.

82
00:04:31.004 --> 00:04:33.724
After 'will', use the base verb: be.

83
00:04:34.533 --> 00:04:37.151
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

84
00:04:37.967 --> 00:04:39.095
Our Big Trip.

85
00:04:39.395 --> 00:04:41.418
We planned our itinerary carefully.

86
00:04:42.433 --> 00:04:45.443
First, we checked our passport and visa requirements.

87
00:04:46.433 --> 00:04:49.002
We booked accommodation near the city centre.

88
00:04:50.000 --> 00:04:53.787
After a short layover in Bangkok, we will reach our destination.

89
00:04:54.800 --> 00:04:58.518
I'm sure the sightseeing will be great, and I will buy many souvenirs!

90
00:04:59.633 --> 00:05:03.438
Part five: quiz. Three questions. Are you ready?

91
00:05:04.283 --> 00:05:06.213
I think the trip blank be fun.

92
00:05:06.513 --> 00:05:09.400
A, will. B, is. C, are.

93
00:05:12.967 --> 00:05:14.966
The answer is A: will.

94
00:05:16.117 --> 00:05:18.732
A short stop between two flights is a blank.

95
00:05:19.032 --> 00:05:22.395
A, layover. B, souvenir. C, visa.

96
00:05:25.933 --> 00:05:28.142
The answer is A: layover.

97
00:05:29.283 --> 00:05:31.341
The place you are travelling to is your blank.

98
00:05:31.641 --> 00:05:35.585
A, destination. B, departure. C, itinerary.

99
00:05:39.133 --> 00:05:41.214
The answer is A: destination.

100
00:05:42.400 --> 00:05:45.586
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

101
00:05:46.450 --> 00:05:48.995
Describe a place you would love to travel to.

102
00:05:57.783 --> 00:05:59.168
Now listen to Visal.

103
00:05:59.468 --> 00:06:08.090
I would love to travel to Korea. I think it will be exciting. I will visit Seoul, try street food and buy souvenirs for my family.

104
00:06:08.390 --> 00:06:10.041
Excellent answer, Visal!

105
00:06:10.950 --> 00:06:15.564
Great work! Now you can use twelve new words and future with will for predictions.

106
00:06:15.864 --> 00:06:20.943
Today's value is open-mindedness. Be open to new places, people and ideas.

107
00:06:21.243 --> 00:06:23.838
See you in Unit fourteen. Goodbye!

108
00:06:24.138 --> 00:06:26.871
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

